                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Quad Cities IA IL",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 3 at 8:34PM CST until November 5 at 2:00PM CST by NWS Quad Cities IA IL",
                "description": "...The Flood Watch continues for the following rivers in Iowa...\n\nEnglish River at Kalona affecting Washington and Johnson Counties.\n\n.Heavy rainfall that feel in the past few days may produce flooding\non portions of the Iowa, English, and North Skunk Rivers.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding is possible.\n\n* WHERE...English River at Kalona.\n\n* WHEN...From late Wednesday night to Thursday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 14.0 feet, Agricultural land along the river begins to\nflood.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:00 PM CST Tuesday the stage was 8.2 feet.\n- Forecast...Flood stage may be reached early Thursday morning.\n- Flood stage is 14.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "If you are in the watch area, remain alert to possible flooding.\n\nResidents and those with interests near the river should monitor\nrising water levels and be prepared for possible Flood Warnings.\n\nThe next statement will be issued by Wednesday evening.",
